   "evidence": "In `./mathlib`, grep for `theorem (isInvertible|inverse)_(mul|lsmul|smul)` finds only the `Ring.inverse` lemmas in Algebra/GroupWithZero/Units/Basic.lean, and grep for `IsInvertible.*mul` and `inverse.*ContinuousLinearMap.mul` finds nothing, so Mathlib lacks this fact. The helper's only call sites are Isothermal.lean:471-480, where it builds exactly these two statements.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Analysis/Complex/Beltrami/Isothermal.lean",
   "fix": "Replace it with public characteristic lemmas in a general file, e.g. `ContinuousLinearMap.isInvertible_mul (hz : z \u2260 0)` and `ContinuousLinearMap.inverse_mul : (mul \ud835\udd5c \ud835\udd5c' z).inverse = mul \ud835\udd5c \ud835\udd5c' z\u207b\u00b9` for a normed field `\ud835\udd5c'` (the latter holds for all `z`, since both sides are 0 at `z = 0`). Put them next to the other `ContinuousLinearMap`/`IsInvertible` material under `TauCeti/Topology/Algebra/Module` and use them in `exists_holderOnWith_iteratedFDeriv_normalizer`.",
   "issue": "The private `mul_inv_comp_mul_and_mul_comp_mul_inv` is general infrastructure: its statement mentions only Mathlib types (`ContinuousLinearMap.mul \u211d \u2102`) and its proof has nothing to do with Beltrami. It exists only so the proof can derive `(mul \u211d \u2102 z).inverse = mul \u211d \u2102 z\u207b\u00b9` and `(mul \u211d \u2102 z).IsInvertible` inline (lines 471-480).",
